        "original_id": "53cf7f87-5d1c-52f4-a6a9-dab1a307bcf6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Éluard, Georges Bataille\n- Works: Capitale de la douleur\n- Movements: Surrealism\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Éluard was born as Eugène Émile Paul Grindel on 14 December 1895.\n- Georges Bataille was born as Georges Albert Maurice Victor Bataille on 10 September 1897.\n- Paul Éluard was a French poet and one of the founders of the surrealist movement.\n- Capitale de la douleur is a book of poems by French surrealist poet Paul Éluard.\n- Georges Bataille was a French intellectual and literary figure who worked in literature, philosophy, anthropology, economics, sociology, and history of art.\n- Paul Éluard died on 18 November 1952.\n- Georges Bataille died on 9 July 1962.",
